{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It is the complement of the lexicographically greatest maximum independent set, not of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"least one: the least vertex of a symmetric difference is in one cover exactly when it is in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the other cover’s complement. That set is found as in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", with each choice the other way round: the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"core pass on a bipartite component leaves out each vertex it decides, a complete component","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keeps its greatest vertex, and any other component deletes a vertex whenever a maximum set","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"without it remains, with the reductions taking a simplicial vertex greater than all its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"neighbours. The cost is that of ","type":"text"},{"code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": O(m √n) on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bipartite components, and up to c exponential searches on a component of c vertices the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reductions do not settle. The search does not check for task cancellation.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstminimumvertexcover()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P8CoveringE40lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCoverSay0G0QzGyF","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","modules":[{"name":"Covering","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"ExactCovering.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Covering\/ExactCovering.swift#L1739"},"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"title":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover()","symbolKind":"method"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"The lexicographically first minimum vertex cover: of the smallest vertex covers, the least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by vertex index (the rule of ","type":"text"},{"code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": of two covers","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of one size, the lesser hol